{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, etc.</b> The reason it did not begin to say ״וַיֹּאמֶר ה׳ אֶל אַבְרָם אַחֲרֵי״ and so on, may be intended to convey that since Scripture said ״וַיֹּאמֶר אַבְרָם אֶל לוֹט וְגוֹ׳ הִפָּרֶד נָא״ and so on, and the wicked man separated from him, Scripture adds to say that HaShem too was sitting and watching for this thing, and immediately, as soon as the wicked man departed, He spoke to him and showed him the land. And this is what He said to him (Genesis 12:1): ״אֲשֶׁר אַרְאֶךָּ,״ as we explained in its place." "<b>And see from the place.</b> The reason it was necessary to say <b>from the place where you are</b>: here He performed for him a great wonder, that he could see from north to south and from west to east from one place without needing to turn around."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:02.657418432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}